Based on the trace you’ve attached, the “FrameCommittedInBrowser” events for your page are coming through with a processPseudoId in args.data but *no* processId.  In the current implementation, findMainFramePidTids does:

  • collects all FrameCommittedInBrowser events for the main frame  
  • maps each event to e.args.data.processId  
  • falls back to the starting PID only if *no* FrameCommittedInBrowser events were seen  

Because processId is missing, the map produces [undefined], which then causes the lookup for the CrRendererMain thread to fail and throw “Unable to determine tid for renderer process.”

We can fix this by falling back to the event’s own evt.pid when args.data.processId is undefined.  That pid is in fact the renderer’s OS‐level pid and will match the subsequent thread_name metadata event.

Below is a single *SEARCH/REPLACE* patch in  
  core/lib/tracehouse/trace-processor.js

```javascript
### core/lib/tracehouse/trace-processor.js
